# SMART MIX (0.16.23, a settings page after SMART DJ): how a SMART DJ set goes from piece to piece. A PEAK set (short grooves), Endless, Journey ANY:
# once a piece has had its round, the groove after its drop mixes into the next piece on a phrase line. Each transition forced in turn (txforce):
# FILTER (the high-pass rising out, the low-pass opening in), BASS SWAP (the bass out before and after the swap), DRUMS FIRST (the new piece's drums
# alone, then all in), LOOP ROLL (the beat repeats in the last bar); each time a new piece, its own round after.
seed 0
wait 3000
press HOME
wait 800
release HOME
wait 100
turn SELECT 4
wait 100
expect fxpage 36
spin K2 2
spin K3 2
wait 50
expect fxs101 4
expect fxs102 2
spin SELECT 1
wait 100
expect fxpage 37
spin K1 1
wait 50
expect fxs104 2
shot mix_page.png
tap FX
wait 200
# START SET; FILTER
txforce 2
press SEL
tap PLAY
release SEL
wait 500
expect djon 1
waitfor tx 2 300000
expect txin 0
wait 6000
expect fxk0 >5
press HOME
wait 800
release HOME
wait 100
turn SELECT 5
wait 100
expect fxpage 37
shot mix_out.png
tap FX
wait 200
waitfor txin 1 30000
wait 200
expect fxk0 <0
waitfor tx 0 40000
wait 2000
expect fxk0 0
expect gnrun >0
# BASS SWAP: the bass out for the outgoing piece's last bars and the incoming's first
txforce 3
waitfor tx 3 400000
waitfor txm 16 30000
wait 100
expect entrkmute 16
waitfor txin 1 30000
expect txm 16
waitfor tx 0 30000
wait 100
expect txm 0
expect entrkmute 0
# DRUMS FIRST: the new piece's drums alone, then the rest on the phrase
txforce 4
waitfor tx 4 400000
waitfor txin 1 40000
wait 100
expect txm 240
expect entrkmute 240
tap HOME
wait 200
shot mix_drumsfirst.png
tap HOME
wait 200
waitfor tx 0 30000
wait 100
expect entrkmute 0
# LOOP ROLL: the beat repeats in the outgoing piece's last bar, then the new piece
txforce 6
waitfor tx 6 400000
waitfor fxbit1 1 40000
waitfor tx 0 10000
expect fxbit1 0
# stopped: nothing of a mix left
txforce -1
tap PLAY
wait 500
expect tx 0
expect txm 0
